### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. State set + order (2 states in the specimen) — per state: label, enslaved count, free count, elector count, tagged flag (which tile carries the clause frame + tag).
2. Icon — presence, fraction split (3/5), icon colours, banner text, banner colours.
3. Tile geometry — tile size, positions/gap, silhouette presence (generic silhouette path per state is data, drawn from CONFIG points — NOT a traced frame: silhouettes are simplified polygons named in CONFIG).
4. Frame — tagged tile's frame width/colour, draw duration.
5. Tag — text, tilt angle, colours, position on the frame corner.
6. Population lines — row labels ("Enslaved people:" / "Free people:"), number formatting (comma-grouped), label/number font sizes, row colours (enslaved numerals in frame orange, free numerals in ink).
7. Squares — per-state elector count, grid columns, square size/pitch, fill colour, per-square stagger + fade duration, numeral text/size (numeral = the count itself, derived).
8. Timing — icon hold/exit, tile start/duration/stagger, free start/duration, frame start/duration, tag start/duration, squares start/stagger/fade, final hold, total duration.
9. Palette — paper ground, tile slate, tile-name pale, frame/tag orange, banner red/teal, icon orange/dark, square black, ink, muted label grey.
10. Easing — per-phase easing names.

### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
- A1 §2 typography precedent (runtime sampling of config-rendered text): NOT APPLICABLE — no particle typography; all text is SVG text rendered from CONFIG strings/numbers, the same config-driven principle in its DOM/SVG form. Reason stated here per A9.5.
- A5 Owner Cures 1–2 (intensity separation · phrase exclusivity): NOT APPLICABLE as particle/sequence cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogous separation here is construction-level: the tagged tile is separated by a *frame + tag* (a different kind of mark), never by intensity alone — priced in Plan. Phase exclusivity DOES apply in its sequencing form: each sub-beat's landing completes before the next begins (phase-order invariant, §2.1).
- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool exists in this technique.
- Family: Packet #12 counting siblings (T208 paired dot counts · T210 threshold grid map · T212 margin bar field) — count-board geometry from CONFIG arrays is the family's demonstrated construction; T212's filed lesson (receipt-form discipline, A12/A13) is carried into §2.4 planning.

